11.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The ESA rules (right to disconnect policy under the 2021 Act; electronic monitoring policy under the 2022 Act) require a written policy only for employers that have 25+ employees on 1 January of the relevant year; the policy must then be prepared by the statutory deadline for that year and distributed to existing employees within 30 days of preparation/revision and to new hires within 30 days of hire.  

- A, B, D and E all have fewer than 25 employees on 1 Jan 2023, so neither policy is mandatory; any policies they happen to maintain or withhold therefore create no compliance breach on the date in question.  
- C has ~1 000 employees on both 1 Jan 2022 and 1 Jan 2023, so both policies are required. Although C maintains the policies, its practice of revising them monthly yet distributing the revisions only quarterly necessarily exceeds the 30-day distribution window for at least some revisions. That timing violation renders C non-compliant as of 2 Jan 2023.  

Thus C is the only employer that is out of compliance on the stated date.}

