PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority (2,3,4,6,8,9,10,11) still converge on D: 30 employees on 1 Jan 2022 fixes both ESA duties for 2022 (disconnecting policy by ~Mar 2022; electronic-monitoring by 11 Oct 2022) plus distribution; D created only the first and still lacks the second on 2 Jan 2023. Threshold is locked by the Jan-1 snapshot and survives later drops (to 24).  
B (23 employees) and A/E (<25 on both relevant Jan-1 dates) never trigger any duty, so voluntary policies or refusals create no breach. C states “appropriately distributed,” so quarterly cadence satisfies the 30-day rule on its face.  
Round-1 dissent (1,5,7,12) misapplies the snapshot rule to B or wrongly claims voluntary policies impose distribution duties; no factual disputes remain. D is the sole ongoing violation.}

