PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Majority (now 2,3,4,6,8,9,10,11) still converges on D: 30 employees on 1 Jan 2022 snapshot locks both ESA duties (disconnect policy by ~Mar/Jun 2022; electronic-monitoring policy by 11 Oct 2022) for full calendar year; D never created the latter, creating ongoing breach on 2 Jan 2023. Head-count drops post-snapshot do not extinguish obligation. C’s “appropriately distributed” language treated as satisfying 30-day rule despite monthly revisions. B (23 employees) and A/E remain below every Jan 1 threshold so no statutory duty; voluntary policies create no breach.  
Minority shift to B (colleagues 1,5,7,12) argues explicit refusal to distribute even voluntary policies to new hires violates absolute distribution rule with no cost exception.  
Unresolved: whether voluntary policies below threshold trigger distribution duties; exact 30-day language vs. “appropriately.” No material errors in facts or dates noted. My view unchanged: D is sole clear mandatory violation.}

